<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<chapter xml:id="ch-season4" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
    <title>Season 4: Decimal Numbers and Introductory Percents </title>
    <introduction>
        <p>
           Like fractions, decimal numbers are also used to represent portions of a whole. 
           While fractions arise most commonly in construction and baking, decimals are used most often when dealing with money. 
           In this season, we will learn how to perform basic calculations involving decimals, how to compare two decimal numbers, 
           and how to convert between fractions and decimals. We will also learn how to calculate percents using decimal numbers. 
        </p>
    </introduction>

